# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps the layer cache useful: the api stage
# does `COPY . .`, so anything reaching the context invalidates the publish layer when it changes.
# Without this file a docs typo busted the cached .NET build.
#
# Deliberately conservative — only paths that cannot affect `dotnet publish src/Platform.Api` or the
# web build are listed. The test projects stay in: the solution file references them, and shaving a
# cached layer isn't worth reasoning about MSBuild's project graph.

# Git metadata. Large, and changes on literally every commit.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# CI / tooling config — never read by the build.
.github
.claude
.vscode
.vs
.idea

# Build outputs. Present on a developer machine, and would otherwise be copied into the image (or
# shadow what the build produces).
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/TestResults
**/.vite

# The documentation site: its own Vite app, unrelated to the container.
docs
notes

# Local environment overrides must never be baked into an image.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise.
**/*.user
**/*.suo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Compose and container definitions — the image doesn't build itself.
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Markdown at the repo root (README, LICENSE and friends).
*.md
LICENSE
